postfix-dane-policy is a small socketmap service for Postfix
smtp_tls_policy_maps. It answers "dane-only" for next-hop domains whose
MX records and MX host TLSA records are DNSSEC-validated, and NOTFOUND
otherwise, so an MTA-STS resolver or the global TLS security level
applies next. DNS failures make Postfix defer instead of downgrading.

Together with smtp_tls_security_level = verify this gives the outbound
policy "DANE if published, else MTA-STS, else a CA-verified certificate,
never plaintext".
